But let me tell you one thing, okay?

00:36:09.940 --> 00:36:14.720
This is a game that, if you haven't played it yet, you, you missed.

00:36:15.000 --> 00:36:17.080
You know, you missed the window of opportunity.

00:36:17.580 --> 00:36:20.240
Games have evolved a lot further from here.

00:36:21.080 --> 00:36:25.820
And, uh, this was a game that was probably very fun and family friendly.

00:36:26.280 --> 00:36:37.440
Like, you know, something, something I could actually see in the 80s, like, at like a, you know, at a party bringing out and like trying each other's skills and seeing who could, you know, who can actually score higher.

00:36:37.560 --> 00:36:38.720
Like, we always joke about high scores.

00:36:38.720 --> 00:36:44.020
But I feel like this one is so fast and so simple and anybody can do it that I feel like that was the appeal.

00:36:44.020 --> 00:36:49.720
You also cannot progress in this game until you beat a moderately high high score.

00:36:50.000 --> 00:36:51.880
So high scores did mean something in this game.

00:36:52.040 --> 00:36:55.120
Yeah, that's true. But if you were doing like human versus human...

00:36:55.120 --> 00:36:59.920
Yeah. And I just think like, you know, it's kind of sad for me to say that.

00:37:00.080 --> 00:37:03.340
I think like NES enthusiasts should definitely go play it.

00:37:03.500 --> 00:37:04.660
It's definitely a play it game.

00:37:04.940 --> 00:37:15.880
The reason why it's not essential though is not just because Konami keeps pumping out like new versions of these that just improve concepts and make, you know, make the game, the gameplay mechanics a little more interesting.

00:37:15.880 --> 00:37:26.080
It's also just that like, what it breaks down to is seven mini games, you know, that can be experienced very fast and don't need to be experienced again.

00:37:26.480 --> 00:37:31.800
It's not like I'm going to be losing sleep over the fact that I didn't get the Javelin world record.

00:37:31.980 --> 00:37:35.440
Yeah, you would need to just want to keep improving in this game.

00:37:35.540 --> 00:37:39.600
And it just seems like a very basic thing to try to improve in.

00:37:39.760 --> 00:37:40.720
I don't know. Yeah.

00:37:40.880 --> 00:37:44.200
And so for that, I just, I can't get on the board with people saying it's essential.

00:37:44.200 --> 00:37:45.520
It was definitely influential.

00:37:45.820 --> 00:37:46.840
I will agree with that.

00:37:47.120 --> 00:37:53.520
Um, and I think especially in 1983 when it was in the arcade, like you would have seen a lot of people gathering towards it.

00:37:53.640 --> 00:37:58.140
But today, nah, you know, if you're not an NES enthusiast, skip it altogether.

00:37:58.400 --> 00:38:05.620
But if you're into playing these games, I would definitely like think about the historical context of it all too when you're playing it.

00:38:05.740 --> 00:38:08.200
